{
  "schema_version": "0.19.0",
  "language": "en",
  "text": "proprium.corporis-christi-epistola",
  "about": "The Epistle of the feast of the Most Holy Body of Christ, 1 Corinthians 11:23–29. Saint Paul hands on the institution of the Eucharist and warns against receiving the Lord's Body and Blood unworthily.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Brethren: I received from the Lord that which I also delivered unto you: that the Lord Jesus, on the night in which He was betrayed, took bread, and giving thanks broke it and said: Take ye and eat; this is My Body, which shall be delivered for you. Do this in remembrance of Me." },
    "s02": { "translation": "In like manner He took the chalice also, after He had supped, saying: This chalice is the New Testament in My Blood. Do this, as often as ye shall drink, in remembrance of Me." },
    "s03": { "translation": "For as often as ye shall eat this bread and drink the chalice, ye shall proclaim the death of the Lord until He come." },
    "s04": { "translation": "Therefore whosoever shall eat this bread or drink the chalice of the Lord unworthily shall be guilty of the Body and Blood of the Lord." },
    "s05": { "translation": "But let a man prove himself, and so let him eat of that bread and drink of the chalice." },
    "s06": { "translation": "For he that eateth and drinketh unworthily eateth and drinketh judgment to himself, not discerning the Body of the Lord." }
  },
